t)"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.43072,"w":0.59307,"h":0.02899,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Solution (a) In the coordinate system we have chosen, s measures height from the ground up, so the"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.46227,"w":0.59301,"h":0.06267,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"velocity is positive on the way up and negative on the way down. The instant the rock is at its highest point is the one instant during the flight when the velocity is 0. To find the maximum height, all we need to do is to find when y = 0 and evaluate s at this time. At any time t during the rock’s motion, its velocity is"},{"x":0.12641,"y":0.49408,"w":0.02908,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"s = 0"},{"x":0.17601,"y":0.51524,"w":0.01453,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"(a)"},{"x":0.52892,"y":0.53534,"w":0.24993,"h":0.03052,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dt (160t - 16t2) = 160 - 32t ft>sec."},{"x":0.45672,"y":0.53857,"w":0.04766,"h":0.01999,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"y = ds"},{"x":0.49079,"y":0.53857,"w":0.04856,"h":0.02727,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dt = d"},{"x":0.06398,"y":0.54098,"w":0.01857,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"s, y"},{"x":0.05939,"y":0.56158,"w":0.01963,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"400"},{"x":0.21096,"y":0.56443,"w":0.08587,"h":0.01216,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"s = 160t − 16t2"},{"x":0.32333,"y":0.58031,"w":0.19821,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The velocity is zero when"},{"x":0.49561,"y":0.60265,"w":0.24437,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"160 - 32t = 0 or t = 5sec."},{"x":0.05939,"y":0.61223,"w":0.01963,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"160"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.62567,"w":0.24053,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The rock’s height at t = 5sec is"},{"x":0.4315,"y":0.64422,"w":0.37258,"h":0.01982,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"smax = s(5) = 160(5) - 16(5)2 = 800 - 400 = 400 ft."},{"x":0.07247,"y":0.64506,"w":0.22947,"h":0.0173,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"t 0"},{"x":0.16892,"y":0.65213,"w":0.09946,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"5 10"},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.6724,"w":0.5931,"h":0.03197,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"See Figure 3.18b. (b) To find the rock’s velocity at 256 ft on the way up and again on the way down, we first"},{"x":0.13172,"y":0.67283,"w":0.11162,"h":0.0218,"fs":0.01023,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"y = = 160 − 32t ds dt"},{"x":0.04849,"y":0.67919,"w":0.03053,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"−160"},{"x":0.18306,"y":0.70032,"w":0.01526,"h":0.01023,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"(b)"},{"x":0.35276,"y":0.70691,"w":0.21764,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"find the two values of t for which"},{"x":0.04849,"y":0.72128,"w":0.25985,"h":0.10435,"fs":0.01151,"n":8,"k":1,"t":"FIGURE 3.18 (a) The rock in Example 4. (b) The graphs of s and y as functions of time; s is largest when y = ds>dt = 0. The graph of s is not the path of the rock: It is a plot of height versus time. The slope of the plot is the rock’s velocity, graphed here as a straight line."},{"x":0.52808,"y":0.72479,"w":0.1794,"h":0.01795,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"s(t) = 160t - 16t2 = 256."},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.7568,"w":0.23781,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"To solve this equation, we write"},{"x":0.50451,"y":0.77466,"w":0.16171,"h":0.05632,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"16t2 - 160t + 256 = 0 16(t2 - 10t + 16) = 0 (t - 2)(t - 8) = 0"},{"x":0.62917,"y":0.83669,"w":0.13217,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"t = 2sec, t = 8sec."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.86039,"w":0.5931,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The rock is 256 ft above the ground 2 sec after the explosion and again 8 sec after the"},{"x":0.35277,"y":0.87574,"w":0.32453,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"explosion. The rock’s velocities at these times are"},{"x":0.46599,"y":0.89216,"w":0.33386,"h":0.04241,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"y(2) = 160 - 32(2) = 160 - 64 = 96 ft>sec. y(8) = 160 - 32(8) = 160 - 256 = -96 ft>sec."}]}